# Veetee VT420 132-column — the narrow companion of veetee-vt420-10x16, on
# the 6x16 dot cell DEC terminals use for 132 columns. The glyph body is
# columns 1-4 (1-5 for the widest letters); rows match the 80-column font.
# Line drawing meets at column 2, row 7. Characters missing here are
# derived from the 80-column font when the font set loads.
#
# Copyright 2026 The veetee Authors. Licensed under the SIL Open Font
# License, Version 1.1 (see OFL.txt).
#
# Format: "cell W H", then for each glyph a "U+XXXX" line followed by H
# rows of W characters, "#" for a lit dot and "." for dark.

